Write a command to run the app

Usage statistics
To run a Spring Boot application, you typically use Maven or Gradle. Assuming your project uses Maven, the command to run the application is:

bash


./mvnw spring-boot:run
This command uses the Maven Wrapper (mvnw) to execute the Spring Boot application. Make sure you are in the root directory of your project where the pom.xml file is located when you run this command.

If your project uses Gradle, the command would be:

bash


./gradlew bootRun
Again, ensure you are in the root directory of your project where the build.gradle file is located. Adjust the command based on the build tool your project is configured with.